# One full batch of the GPU apps: 2000 stars, NOSTOS_BATCH_STARS' default, so the app runs one batch of 200,000 star-clone
# pairs, about a minute or two on a mid-range GPU (comment in src/main_nostos_gpu_boinc.cpp). The production GPU work
# unit is 20,000 stars, ten such batches; one batch exercises the same code and is quick enough to repeat. For the CUDA
# and OpenCL builds of build_variant.sh only: on the CPU app it would take about 1.5 hours, and a Mac cannot run the
# GPU apps (they need fp64, Apple's GPUs have none), so mac_ab.sh skips it. Production threshold, two real stars. A
# change of the batch size or the kernel slice length (NOSTOS_BATCH_STARS, NOSTOS_STEPS_PER_LAUNCH, set in a wrapper
# script that is the label's binary) needs more stars than one batch to show anything: copy this file and raise stars.
iso oumuamua
stars 2000
anchors 2
star_seed 20261104
seed_base 1
time_myr -100
steps 100000
threshold_pc 50
apps gpu
